It is late in the afternoon.
Now I walk home to my apartment.
I walk an easy way.
I just follow the long road.
The road is completely straight.
I walk along the water.
Finally I turn away from the water.
Now I walk into the city again.
Then I walk past the bakery.
It still smells of coffee.
A little later I see the park.
At the park I turn right.
I do not ask anyone for directions.
I find the way all by myself.
A little later I see my own street.
Finally I stand at my front door.
From the door I look back down the street.
Now I know my way home.
